pthreads: exit leaves a crashed thread, and a past time is a timeout at once

At exit, __pthread_Exit_Func joins every thread so that no code is unloaded
under one that still runs. A thread that crashed never ends: exec's trap
handling (Kickstart's default trap code, GFOpenKick's included) sends a task
that took a CPU exception to Wait(0) for good, and the thread's finished
flag is never set. The join then waited for ever, and the program never
returned to the Shell. GFOpenBrowser's obcore-view hung this way on reddit.com
whenever reCAPTCHA's Web Worker thread crashed (WTFCrash: a write to
0xBBADBEEF, then a trap).

Exit now joins through ExitJoin(). It checks the thread every two ticks
(Delay(2)), under thread_sem:
- ended: joined as before;
- not started yet: waits for it to start;
- its task in TS_WAIT with tc_SigWait 0: left behind. No Signal() can wake
  a Wait(0), so the task never runs again and the code unloaded under it is
  never reached. Its task and stack are not freed.
finished is set under thread_sem before a thread's task goes, so while
finished is clear the task is still there to look at. A thread that crashes
while exit waits for it is caught on the next check.

pthread_cond_timedwait with an absolute time already past (or now) waited
for ever. The time is turned into an interval for timer.device by
subtracting gettimeofday(), and timer.device takes the interval as
unsigned, so a negative one never ended. WTF::sleep() (WebKit's
ParkingLot, through ThreadCondition::timedWait) never returned on the
Amiga because of this. A negative or zero interval is now one microsecond,
so the wait times out at once.

tests/pthreads/exitpark.c shows both. On a lab copy of Instance-32
(GFOpenKick, AC090), built against 0001-0006 and against 0001-0007:

| case | 0001-0006 | 0001-0007 |
|---|---|---|
| a thread crashes (write to 0xBBADBEEF, then a trap); main returns | no return (x1) | returned, RC 0 (x4) |
| a thread ends; exit joins it | returned | returned |
| timedwait, absolute time 2 s in the past | never returned | ETIMEDOUT after 0 ms |
| timedwait, 200 ms ahead | not reached | ETIMEDOUT after 200 ms |

joinsig.c (0006) still passes with 0007.

